    <h3>Scenarios Theory</h3>
    <p> To build a robust understanding of the headroom for growth, our forecasting model assesses three different scenarios.</p>
    <div class="liststyle">
      <ul>
        <li><span>Scenario A:What's the headroom for  , assuming our share remains the same and we grow through category tailwinds?</span></li>
        <li><span>Scenario B: What's the theoretical headroom for  , assuming we had 100% share of the future value pool size?</span></li>
        <li><span>Scenario C: What's the maximum headroom for growth, for the TBA category?</span></li>
        <li><span>The Scenarios: Theory page will provide an overview of what each of these three scenarios is and what each output means.</span></li>
      </ul>
     </div>
  
   <p>You'll find the outputs for how the model has assessed each scenario within the Decision Matrix. The Decision Matrix can be found in 
the Final Forecast Model tab.</p>
<button class="btn golink hover"><a data-toggle="tab" href="##home"><img src="images/go.png" alt="go" /></a></button>
</div>
